# Dual-Strike Notification System: Expo Push + Existing WebSocket

Add Expo Push Notifications as an offline safety net alongside the existing Socket.IO real-time system. When the app is open, push banners are silently muted (WebSocket handles everything). When the app is closed/backgrounded, push notifications drop a banner that deep-links the user to the correct screen.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Push Notifications CANNOT be tested on Expo Web.** Expo Push Notifications rely on native APNs (iOS) and FCM (Android) services. The `expo-notifications` module returns `null` for push tokens on web and all notification APIs are no-ops. You **must** use a physical Android/iOS device via Expo Go or a development build. An Android emulator with Google Play Services will also work for FCM.

> [!WARNING]
> **Package installation**: I will run the install commands for both frontend (`expo install`) and backend (`npm install`) directly. Both codebases will gain new dependencies.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Your existing WebSocket code is NEVER touched.** The push system is built entirely alongside it — new files, new fields, additive-only edits to existing backend controllers.

