### Phase 6: Frontend — Push Token Hook

#### [NEW] [usePushNotifications.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sriharish/Desktop/FIXI-FRONTEND/homezyy/homezyy/hooks/usePushNotifications.ts)
A reusable hook that:
1. Checks if running on a physical device (`expo-device`)
2. Requests notification permissions
3. Calls `getExpoPushTokenAsync()` to get the Expo Push Token
4. Sends it to `POST /push-token/register` via the existing axios instance
5. Returns the token and any error state
6. Is a no-op on web (gracefully skips)

This hook is called once globally — it does NOT interfere with the existing `SocketContext`.

