### Phase 7: Frontend — Traffic Cop + Deep-Link Router

#### [MODIFY] [_layout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Sriharish/Desktop/FIXI-FRONTEND/homezyy/homezyy/app/_layout.tsx)
Add the following **alongside** the existing providers (AuthProvider, SocketProvider):

1. **Import and call `usePushNotifications()`** to register the token on app load.

2. **Set `Notifications.setNotificationHandler()`** — the Traffic Cop:
   ```js
   Notifications.setNotificationHandler({
     handleNotification: async () => ({
       shouldShowAlert: false,   // SUPPRESS banner when foreground
       shouldPlaySound: false,
       shouldSetBadge: false,
     }),
   });
   ```
   This runs at module level (outside the component). When the app is in the foreground, WebSocket handles everything — push banners are silently eaten.

3. **`addNotificationResponseReceivedListener`** — Deep-link router:
   When a user taps a background/killed notification, this listener fires and reads `notification.request.content.data.screen` to call `router.push(screen)`.

#### Structure of the modified `_layout.tsx`:
```
// Module level: setNotificationHandler (Traffic Cop)
// Inside RootLayout:
//   - usePushNotifications() → registers token
//   - useEffect with addNotificationResponseReceivedListener → handles tap routing
//   - Everything else (AuthProvider, SocketProvider, Stack, SocketOverlay) stays UNTOUCHED
```

