## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `node -e "require('./utils/sendPushNotification')"` in backend to verify the utility loads without errors.
- Start backend with `npm start` and confirm no crashes.
- Start frontend with `npx expo start` and confirm no build errors.

### Manual Verification (Physical Device Required)
- Install Expo Go on a physical Android device.
- Run `npx expo start` and scan the QR code.
- Login as a technician → verify the push token is registered (check MongoDB `technicians` collection for `pushToken` field).
- From a second device/Postman, create a booking invite → verify the technician receives a push notification when the app is backgrounded.
- Tap the notification → verify it routes to the Home screen.
- Test Trigger 2 and 3 similarly.

### Web Testing Limitation
> [!CAUTION]
> **You CANNOT test push notifications on Expo Web.** The `expo-notifications` module is a native-only API. On web, `getExpoPushTokenAsync()` returns null and all notification handlers are no-ops. The hook is written to gracefully skip on web, so your web dev workflow is unaffected — but to actually test push, you need a physical device or Android emulator with Google Play Services.
